[{"id":54627,"sender_id":56,"sender_full_name":"jamievicary","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/5d4cb43d795a03148f8552151d9af219?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Greater-than.20and.20less-than/near/54627\">#1</a> Hi,</p>\n<p>How can I enter a greater-than symbol in a latex expression in an nLab page? When I do it in the usual way I get the error ‘unknown character’. 15 minutes of looking at help pages has not enlightened me.</p>\n<p>Cheers\nJamie</p>","timestamp":1448834350,"subject":"Greater-than and less-than","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":54628,"sender_id":138,"sender_full_name":"Zhen Lin","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/5284233bbaf108722eea4bbf89fdeda2?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Greater-than.20and.20less-than/near/54628\">#2</a> Use <code>\\lt</code> and <code>\\gt</code> instead. It seems that angle brackets get misinterpreted as XML.</p>","timestamp":1448834868,"subject":"Greater-than and less-than","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":54629,"sender_id":56,"sender_full_name":"jamievicary","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/5d4cb43d795a03148f8552151d9af219?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Greater-than.20and.20less-than/near/54629\">#3</a> Very nice, thanks.</p>","timestamp":1448836237,"subject":"Greater-than and less-than","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":54630,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Greater-than.20and.20less-than/near/54630\">#4</a> I added this to the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/FAQ\">FAQ</a>.</p>","timestamp":1448857260,"subject":"Greater-than and less-than","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":54635,"sender_id":78,"sender_full_name":"RodMcGuire","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/93dc0f9f03cdabb6b19a1522bd94c69f?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Greater-than.20and.20less-than/near/54635\">#5</a> The documentation of how to in the nLab is rather hit and miss.</p>\n<p>I’ve sometimes just resorted to finding an example in the nLab or nForum.</p>\n<p>For your case, the page <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/preorder\">preorder</a> contains the text:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A preorder (also sometimes called a quasi-order, especially if one works with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>&lt;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lt</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.5782em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&lt;</span></span></span></span> instead of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\leq</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7719em;vertical-align:-0.136em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span></span></span></span>) …</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>If you just copy and paste part of that (at least in FIrefox) you get the text:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>with &lt;\\lt instead of ≤\\leq</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>which gives the rendering followed by the underlying iTeX.</p>\n<p>Also, if you want to do tests to figure out how to get some rendering, the nForum is often better than the nLab because it does give previews and you don’t have to click <code>Add your comments</code> while the nLab requires <code>Submit</code> to see the rendering.</p>","timestamp":1448907303,"subject":"Greater-than and less-than","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":54637,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Greater-than.20and.20less-than/near/54637\">#6</a> Fortunately, the nLab is a wiki, including its self-documentation.  So once you figure something out, you can improve the documentation yourself for the benefit of future editors!  (-:</p>","timestamp":1448927418,"subject":"Greater-than and less-than","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]}]